# Prefer Mantine

YARK’s renderer is a **Mantine** app (theme + tokens in
`src/renderer/src/shared/theme/`). Prefer Mantine’s built-in components and props
before inventing custom markup or CSS for the same job.

Full guidance: [docs/design-system.md](../../docs/design-system.md).

## Quick rules

- Use Mantine for wizards/modals (`Modal`, `Stepper`), forms (`TextInput`,
  `Select`, `Checkbox`, `Switch`, `NumberInput`), feedback (`Alert`, `Tooltip`,
  `Badge`, `Notification`), and layout (`Stack`, `Group`, `SimpleGrid`).
- Match existing patterns: `CreateClusterModal` / `AddServersModal` already use
  `Stepper` (`size="sm"`, `allowNextStepsSelect={false}`).
- Prefer Mantine props (`gap`, `p`, `radius`, `variant`, `size`) + CSS variables
  over one-off hex/px and hand-rolled steppers, tabs, or tooltips.
- Shared YARK atoms (`AppSurfaceCard`, `EmptyState`, `PathField`, …) still win
  when the design system already defines that chrome.
- Custom CSS modules are for feature-specific layout/polish after Mantine +
  shared atoms are exhausted — not for reimplementing Mantine widgets.
